\v 5 He'll take¦319423 Tsidkiyah to Babylon \add ≈where\add* he'll remain until¦319429 \add ≈I've dealt\add* with him. \add ≈No,\add* you all won't¦319441 succeed¦319442 in fighting¦319437 against the \add ≈Babylonians\add*. That is Yahweh's¦319435 declaration.
\p
\v 6 Then Yirmeyah said¦319445: Yahweh¦319450 \add ≈gave\add* me a message¦319448, saying:
\v 7 Listen, your \add cousin\add* Hanamel¦319455 (your uncle¦319459 Shallum's¦319458 son) is coming to \add see\add* you and will \add ≈ask\add* you to buy \add %his\add* field¦319467 in Anatot¦319469, because¦319470 you have the right¦319472 to buy it.
\v 8 Then just as Yahweh \add ≈had said\add*, my \add ≈cousin\add* Hanamel¦319478 came to me in the guards' courtyard¦319486 and¦319476 he \add ≈asked\add* me, “Buy my field¦319494 that is in Anatot¦319497 in the Benyamin¦319501 \add ≈region¦319500\add*, because¦319502 you have the right to inherit it \add ≈so\add* the right to buy it belongs¦319507 to you. Buy it for yourself¦319504.” Then I knew that this was Yahweh's¦319483 message.
\v 9 \add ≈So¦319519\add* I bought¦319519 the field¦319522 in Anatot¦319529 from my \add ≈cousin\add* Hanamel¦319524, and¦319519 I weighed¦319530 out seventeen¦319536 shekels¦319537 of silver for him.
\v 10 Then¦319541 I wrote¦319541 in a scroll and sealed¦319543 it, and had witnesses witness it \add ≈and the weight¦319546 of\add* the silver¦319547 on the scales.
\v 11 Next I took¦319550 \add &that\add* sealed¦319557 purchase¦319554 \add ≈deed\add* with the \add ≈price\add* and¦319550 conditions¦319559, \add ≈as well as an unsealed copy\add*.
\v 12 I gave¦319564 the \add sealed\add* purchase document to Baruk (son of Neriyah, son of Mahseyah¦319577) \add ≈in front of\add* my \add ≈cousin\add* Hanamel¦319579 and¦319564 the witnesses¦319582 who'd \add ≈signed\add* the purchase agreement, as well as all the Judeans who were sitting¦319590 in the guards' courtyard¦319591.
\v 13 Then¦319594 \add still\add* \add ≈in front of them\add*, I \add ≈instructed¦319594\add* Baruk,
\v 14 Yisrael's god¦319606, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦319604 says¦319603 this: Take these¦319612 documents¦319611, both this receipt of purchase¦319615 that's sealed¦319618 and the unsealed copies, and put them into a clay jar so they'll last for a long time¦319629,
\v 15 because¦319633 Yisrael's god¦319638, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦319636 says¦319635 this: Houses, fields¦319643, and vineyards¦319644 will again¦319640 be bought¦319641 in this land.
\s1 Yirmeyah's prayer
\rem /s1 Jeremiah's Prayer; Jeremiah Prays for Understanding
\p
\v 16 After I'd given the purchase¦319658 \add ≈deed\add* to Neriyah's son Baruk, I prayed¦319649 to Yahweh¦319652, saying:
\v 17 Oh no, master¦319668 Yahweh¦319668. Listen, you alone made¦319673 the heavens¦319676 and the earth¦319679 \add ≈by taking action\add* and using your incredible strength¦319680. Nothing you say is too difficult¦319686 for you to do.
\v 18 You show loyal¦319693 commitment to thousands¦319694, and pour people's guilt into their children's¦319701 \add ≈laps\add* after¦319702 them. You are the strong and powerful god¦319703—your name¦319708 is Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦319706.
\v 19 You are \add ≈very wise\add* and \add ≈do incredible things\add*, because your eyes¦319716 are open to all the people's ways—to give each person what their conduct and actions deserve.
\v 20 You did \add ≈miracles and amazing things\add* in Egypt¦319738 \add (Heb. Mitsrayim)\add*, \add ?remembered\add* to this day, and you've¦319745 made a name for yourself¦319747 in Yisrael¦319743 and among¦319744 humankind¦319744.
\v 21 You brought¦319752 your people¦319755 Yisrael¦319758 out from Egypt¦319760 using \add ≈miracles and amazing things\add* and \add ≈by taking action\add* and using your incredible strength, along with great¦319768 terror¦319767.
\v 22 Then¦319770 you gave them this land which¦319776 you had promised¦319778 their¦319779 ancestors¦319779 that¦319776 you'd give them—a land flowing¦319783 with milk and¦319770 honey¦319785.
\v 23 \add ≈So¦319787\add* they entered and¦319787 took¦319788 possession¦319788 of it, \add ≈but¦319787\add* they didn't listen¦319792 to your voice¦319793 or follow your instructions¦319803. They didn't do anything that you'd ordered¦319803 them to do \add ≈so\add* you've¦319808 brought all this calamity¦319813 onto them.
\p
\v 24 Look, the siege mounds¦319817 have \add ≈reached up\add* to the city to capture¦319820 it, and its been \add ≈handed over\add* to the Babylonians \add (Heb. Chaldeans)\add* who've been fighting¦319825 it. Everything you said would happen¦319833 has, including¦319821 \add ≈war\add*, famine¦319829, and deadly diseases, and you're¦319834 there¦319834 watching it.
\v 25 Then¦319837 you yourself told me, ‘Use silver¦319846 to buy yourself a field¦319845, and¦319837 have witnesses witness it, even though this city¦319849 is being \add ≈handed over to the Babylonians\add* \add (Heb. Chaldeans)\add*.’
\rem /s1 God's Assurance of the People's Return; A Prediction of Jerusalem's Fall
\p
\v 26 Then¦319854 Yahweh¦319857 \add ≈gave\add* Yirmeyah¦319860 \add &this\add* message¦319855:
\v 27 Listen, I'm Yahweh¦319865, the god¦319866 of all \add ≈mankind\add*. Is there anything that's too difficult¦319871 for me to do?
\v 28 Therefore Yahweh¦319879 says this, ‘Listen, I'm about¦319881 to \add ≈hand\add* this city¦319884 over to the \add ≈Babylonians\add*—the Babylonian King¦319890 Nebuchadnezzar¦319889 will capture¦319893 it.\x + \xo 32:28: \xt 2Ki 25:1-11; 2Ch 36:17-21.\x*
\v 29 The \add ≈soldiers\add* who are fighting¦319897 against this city will come and set fire to this city and burn it. Those people¦319912 who worship Baal¦319916 on their \add flat\add* roofs¦319915, and who poured¦319917 out drink¦319918 offerings¦319918 to other¦319920 gods in order to provoke¦319922 me, will \add now\add* have their houses¦319910 burnt down
\v 30 because¦319937 the people of Yisrael¦319929 and Yehudah¦319931 have certainly been people who've been doing¦319933 evil \add ≈in front of me\add* since¦319936 their youth¦319936. The people of Israel¦319929 have certainly offended me with the practices \add ≈and activities\add*. That is Yahweh's¦319948 declaration.
\v 31 Yahweh declares that \add the people of\add* this city¦319959 has \add ≈provoked\add* my anger¦319953 and fury since the day that they built¦319965 it, and then right up to the present day, \add ≈so\add* I'll will remove¦319970 it \add right\add* \add ≈out of my sight\add*,
\v 32 \add ≈because of\add* all the wicked things that¦319983 the people¦319978 of Yisrael¦319980 and Yehudah have done¦319984 to provoke¦319985 me—their kings¦319987, princes, priests¦319989, prophets¦319990, and every¦319991 person in Yehudah \add ≈including¦319981\add* Yerushalem's¦319994 inhabitants¦319993.
\v 33 They turned¦319996 their backs to me instead of their faces, even though I had \add ≈eagerly\add* taught¦320001 them. I tried to teach¦320004 them, but¦319996 they wouldn't listen¦320006 \add ≈or\add* receive correction¦320008.
\v 34 They set up their¦320011 detestable¦320011 \add >idols\add* in the house¦320012 that¦320013 is called¦320015 by my name¦320017, \add in order\add* to defile it,\x + \xo 32:34: \xt 2Ki 23:10; Jer 7:30-31; 19:1-6.\x*
\v 35 and they built¦320021 \add ≈hilltop¦320024 shrines¦320024\add* for Baal¦320025 along the Ben-Hinnom Valley¦320031 in order to pass¦320032 their sons¦320035 and daughters¦320038 through¦320032 the fire for Molek¦320039.\x + \xo 32:35: \xt 2Ki 23:10; Jer 7:31.\x* I didn't¦320041 command¦320043 them \add to do that\add*—it¦320045 never entered my mind¦320048 that they should do that detestable thing and so cause¦320053 Yehudah¦320057 to sin¦320053.’\x + \xo 32:35: \xt Lev 18:21.\x*
\s1 Promised restoration
\rem /s1 A Promise of Hope; A Promise of Restoration
\p
\v 36 So now Yisrael's god¦320066 Yahweh¦320065 \add ≈has something to say\add* about this city¦320070 that¦320072 you've all been talking¦320075 about, saying¦320075, ‘It's \add ≈been handed over\add* to the Babylonian king¦320078 \add due to\add* \add ≈war\add*, famine¦320082, and \add ≈deadly diseases\add*.’
\v 37 Listen, I'll¦320085 gather¦320086 them \add back\add* from every land where¦320090 I had banished¦320091 them to in my rage, fury, and great¦320096 anger. I'm about to bring¦320097 them back to this place¦320100 and enable them to live in security¦320103,
\v 38 and then¦320105 they'll be my people¦320107 and I'll¦320109 be their god¦320111.
\v 39 I'll¦320113 give¦320113 them \add ≈a united vision\add* and a single way¦320117 to honour me every day so that it'll \add turn out\add* good¦320124 for them and for their¦320126 descendants after¦320127 them.
\v 40 Then¦320129 I'll make¦320129 a permanent¦320132 agreement¦320131 with them, that I won't¦320134 turn away from doing good to them. I'll set honour for me in their¦320144 \add ≈minds\add*, so that they'll never turn away from me.
\v 41 Then¦320149 I'll \add ≈take pleasure\add* in doing good¦320151 to them. I'll faithfully¦320156 plant¦320153 them in this land with all my heart¦320159 and¦320149 all my life
\v 42 because¦320165 Yahweh¦320169 says¦320168 this, ‘Just as I have brought¦320171 all this great¦320180 disaster on this people¦320174, so too I'll¦320183 bring¦320184 on them all the good¦320190 things that¦320191 I've¦320171 said I'd do for them.
\v 43 Then¦320196 \add people\add* will buy fields¦320197 in this land, about which¦320200 you've been saying¦320203, “This land is ruined, without people or \add even\add* animals¦320208 \add living\add* on it. It's been \add ≈handed over to\add* the \add ≈Babylonians\add*.”
\v 44 They'll use silver¦320214 to buy fields¦320213 and will write¦320216 in sealed scrolls. They'll assemble witnesses¦320220 in the Benyamin¦320223 \add ≈region¦320222\add*, all around Yerushalem¦320225 and Yehudah's¦320227 \add other\add* cities of Judah, in the cities in the hill country¦320229 and in the lowlands, and in the cities of the Negev¦320233, because¦320234 I'll¦320236 \add ≈bring back their¦320239 fortunes\add*. That is Yahweh's¦320242 declaration.
\c 33
\s1 Promised blessings
\rem /s1 Promises of Peace and Prosperity; Another Promise of Hope; Healing after Punishment; Promise of Restoration
\p
\v 1 ⇔Then while Yirmeyah¦320251 was still¦320254 locked in the guards' courtyard¦320256, Yahweh¦320248 \add ≈gave\add* him a second¦320252 message¦320246, saying,
\v 2 Yahweh, the maker \add of the earth\add*, who formed¦320266 \add ≈and established¦320268 it\add* and \add who's known by\add* his name¦320270 Yahweh, says¦320262:
\v 3 Call \add out\add* to me, and I'll answer¦320274 you. I'll tell you \add ≈amazing\add* \add >things\add* that¦320279 you haven't \add previously\add* known \add ≈or understood\add*.
\v 4 \add ≈Yes,\add* Yisrael's god¦320287, Yahweh¦320286, says this about the houses in this city¦320292 and the \add ≈palaces\add* of Yehudah's¦320298 king that¦320299 were torn down \add to be used against\add* the siege ramps and the \add ≈attackers\add*:
\v 5 The \add ≈Babylonians\add* are coming¦320307 to fight¦320308, and to fill¦320312 the houses with the corpses¦320315 of the people that¦320317 I'll kill in my rage¦320321 and fury when I \add ≈turn my back on\add* this city¦320325 because of all their¦320330 wickedness.
\v 6 Listen, I'm about to bring a cure and healing, because I'll¦320332 heal them and will bring bountiful peace and prosperity to them, and \add ?≈justice\add*.
\v 7 I'll \add ≈bring back the fortunes\add* of Yehudah¦320349 and¦320345 Yisrael¦320352—I'll build them up as \add ≈they were before\add*.
\v 8 Then¦320356 I'll purify them from all the \add ≈evil\add* that they've committed against me—I'll pardon all the \add ≈times that they disobeyed\add* me, and¦320356 all the ways that they rebelled¦320374 against me.
\v 9 Then this city will become¦320377 \add an object\add* of joy¦320380 for me—a song of praise¦320381 and honour¦320382 for all the nations¦320384 of the earth¦320385 who'll hear¦320387 about all the good things that I'm going to do for it. Then \add @the people in the city\add* will \add ≈be respectful\add* and tremble¦320398 because of all the good things and the peace and prosperity that I'll¦320394 give to it.
\p
\v 10 Yahweh¦320416 says this: In this place that you're all talking¦320424 about, saying¦320424, “It's desolate—a place where neither people or animals \add live\add*,” in Yehudah's¦320432 cities¦320431 \add ≈including¦320429\add* Yerushalem's¦320434 streets¦320433 that are \add indeed\add* desolate \add ≈with no people or animals around\add*, there'll be heard¦320418 again¦320417
\v 11 the sounds of happiness and \add ≈celebration\add*. \add ≡You'll all hear\add* the sounds of the bride¦320448 and groom, and those¦320452 who bring¦320466 thank offerings to Yahweh's¦320456 \add ≈temple\add* will be heard saying,
\q1 “Give thanks to Commander-in-chief Yahweh,
\q1 because¦320458 Yahweh is good¦320460,
\q1 and his loyal¦320465 commitment lasts forever¦320464!”
\m \add ≈Yes,\add* I'll¦320472 \add ≈restore the fortunes of\add* the land to what they were before, says¦320479 Yahweh.\x + \xo 33:11: \xt 1Ch 16:34; 2Ch 5:13; 7:3; Ezr 3:11; Psa 100:5; 106:1; 107:1; 118:1; 136:1.\x*
\p
\v 12 Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦320486 says¦320485: ‘In this desolate¦320493 place¦320491 where \add ≈no people or animals¦320499\add* \add are living\add*, around all its¦320502 cities¦320502 there'll again¦320488 be pastures¦320503 where shepherds¦320504 \add ≈can rest\add* their flocks¦320506.
\v 13 In¦320511 the cities in the hill country, the lowlands, and the Negev¦320513, in the Benyamin¦320515 \add region¦320514\add*, and all around Yerushalem¦320517 and in Yehudah's¦320519 \add other\add* cities, the flocks¦320522 will again¦320520 pass \add ≈be counted by their shepherds\add*,’ says Yahweh¦320528.
\rem /s1 The Righteous Branch and the Covenant with David
\p
\v 14 Yahweh¦320536 declares: Listen¦320531, \add ≈the time¦320532\add* is coming¦320533 when I'll¦320537 do what I've¦320543 promised for the \add ≈people\add* of Yisrael¦320547 and Yehudah¦320551.
\v 15 In those¦320554 days¦320553 and at that time¦320555, I'll¦320557 make a \add ≈righteous\add* branch¦320559 grow for David¦320558, and he'll \add ≈do¦320561 what's fair and right throughout\add* the land.
\v 16 Yehudah¦320569 will be rescued in those¦320567 days¦320566, and Yerushalem¦320570 will live in security¦320572, because it'll be called, ‘Yahweh¦320579 is \add ≈the one who does what's right¦320581 for us\add*,’
\v 17 because¦320584 Yahweh¦320588 says¦320587 this: ‘\add ≈There'll always be one of David's¦320592 descendants reigning over\add* Yisrael¦320600,\x + \xo 33:17: \xt 2Sam 7:12-16; 1Ki 2:4; 1Ch 17:11-14.\x*
\v 18 and \add ≈there'll always be a Levitical¦320603 priest¦320602 to stand in front¦320608 of\add* me to sacrifice burnt¦320610 offerings, to burn grain¦320612 offerings, and to offer other sacrifices.’\x + \xo 33:18: \xt Num 3:5-10.\x*
\p
\v 19 Then Yahweh¦320625 \add ≈gave\add* Yirmeyah \add &this\add* message¦320623:
\v 20 Yahweh¦320633 says this: ‘If you all can break¦320636 my contract with day and night so that there'll no longer be day or night at their¦320650 proper times,
\v 21 then my agreement with my servant David¦320658 my servant could \add also\add* be broken¦320655, so that he would no longer have a descendant to sit on his throne¦320667. \add ≡The same is true for\add* my agreement with my servants¦320672, the priests¦320671 \add ≈from Levi¦320670 tribe\add*.
\v 22 As the stars in the skies¦320679 can't be counted¦320677, and as the sand \add grains\add* on the seashores can't be measured¦320681, so I'll¦320685 increase¦320685 the descendants of my¦320694 servant¦320690 David¦320689, as well as the Levites¦320693 who \add ≈work for\add* me.’
\p
\v 23 Yahweh¦320701 \add ≈gave\add* Yirmeyah¦320704 \add &this\add* message¦320699:
\v 24 Haven't you \add ≈noticed\add* what this people \add group\add* has declared when they said, ‘The two clans¦320716 that Yahweh¦320719 chose¦320718, now he's rejected¦320721 them’? In that way they despise my people, saying that they no longer \add ≈deserve to be\add* a nation¦320728 \add ≈as far as they're concerned\add*.
\v 25 \add But¦320740\add* \add ≈I,\add* Yahweh¦320734 say this: Didn't I establish the \add permanent\add* contract with day and night¦320740, and determine the laws of \add ≈the universe\add* and \add ≈this planet\add*?
\v 26 \add ≈In the same way,\add* would I \add now\add* reject¦320754 Yakov's descendants and not bring a ruler¦320757 for the descendants of Abraham¦320761, Yitshak, and Yakov out of them. \add No,\add* because¦320764 I'll¦320754 \add ≈restore their¦320770 fortunes\add* and \add ≈show mercy towards\add* them.
\c 34
\s1 The warning for Tsidkiyah/Zedekiah
\rem /s1 Death in Captivity Predicted for Zedekiah; Events under Jehoiakim and Zedekiah; A Warning for Zedekiah; Warning to Zedekiah; A Message for Zedekiah
\p
\v 1 Yahweh¦320782 \add ≈gave\add* this message¦320774 to Yirmeyah when the Babylonian King¦320784 Nebuchadnezzar¦320783, along with all the \add ≈world's\add* kingdoms¦320793, domains, and people¦320799 \add groups\add* under his \add ≈control\add*, was \add ≈attacking\add* Yerushalem¦320803 and \add ≈Yehudah's other\add* cities¦320808, saying:\x + \xo 34:1: \xt 2Ki 25:1-11; 2Ch 36:17-21.\x*
\v 2 Yisrael's god¦320815 Yahweh says to go and speak to Yehudah's¦320823 King¦320822 Tsidkiyah \add (Zedekiah¦320821)\add* and tell him that Yahweh says this: Listen, I'm about¦320830 to \add ≈hand¦320835 this city¦320833 over\add* to the Babylonian king, and he'll \add ≈set it on fire¦320840\add*.
\v 3 You won't¦320843 escape¦320844 from his \add ≈power\add*, because¦320846 you'll definitely be captured¦320847 and \add ≈handed over to him\add* and you'll \add ≈talk face-to-face with\add* the king¦320855 of Babylon as you're \add ≈taken\add* to Babylon.
\v 4 However King¦320873 Tsidkiyah, listen¦320868 to Yahweh's¦320871 message¦320869—you won't¦320880 be \add ≈killed by being run through with a\add* sword¦320882
\v 5 \add but¦320886 actually\add* you'll die¦320885 in peace¦320884. They'll \add ≈cremate\add* your body as was done for your ancestors¦320887, the previous kings¦320888, and they'll mourn¦320900 for you \add saying,\add*, ‘Oh no, master¦320899!’ That's the promise¦320905 that Yahweh¦320899 has declared.
\v 6 \add ≈So\add* the prophet¦320916 Yirmeyah \add ≈passed on\add* all those messages to Yehudah's¦320921 King¦320920 Tsidkiyah in Yerushalem¦320927
\v 7 \add ≈when\add* the Babylonian king's army had attacked Yerushalem¦320936 and Yehudah's¦320941 remaining¦320951 fortified¦320955 cities of Lakish and Azekah¦320948.
\s1 The restoration of slaves
\rem /s1 Treacherous Treatment of Slaves; Deceitful Treatment of Slaves; Freedom for Slaves; Freedom for Hebrew Slaves
\p
\v 8 Yahweh¦320966 \add ≈gave\add* a message¦320958 to Yirmeyah after¦320967 King¦320969 Tsidkiyah had made¦320968 an agreement¦320971 with all the people¦320976 in Yerushalem¦320978 that¦320959 \add ≈they'd free\add*
\v 9 their male and female¦320991 Hebrew slaves—\add ≈no one should¦320983 force a fellow Jew\add* to work¦320996 for them.
\v 10 \add ≈So¦321003\add* all the leaders and people¦321009 \add ≈formally agreed\add* that each person would free their male and female¦321022 slaves, and they \add ≈put it into practice—taking them from their work¦321025\add* and setting them free.
\v 11 \add ≈However,\add* after¦321033 that they \add ≈changed their minds\add* and \add ≈retrieved\add* the male and female slaves that they'd freed, then¦321032 forced¦321046 them to \add ≈work as slaves again\add*.
\p
\v 12 Then Yahweh¦321055 \add ≈gave me\add* \add &this\add* message¦321053 to tell them:
\v 13 Yisrael's god¦321067 Yahweh¦321066 says¦321065 that I personally made¦321070 an agreement¦321071 with your ancestors¦321074 on the day¦321075 that I brought¦321076 them out from \add ≈their lives of slavery¦321081 in\add* Egypt¦321079 \add (Heb. Mitsrayim)\add*. That was when I said that
\v 14 at the end of every¦321088 seven¦321085 years, you all must¦321087 release any fellow Hebrews¦321092 who had sold \add #themselves\add* to you and served¦321097 you for six years, \add ≈releasing them as free people\add*. \add ≈However,\add* your ancestors¦321106 did not listen¦321105 to me or \add ≈show any desire to obey\add* me.\x + \xo 34:14: \xt Exo 21:2; Deu 15:12.\x*
\v 15 \add ≈Now\add* \add recently,\add* you yourselves repented and¦321114 began to do what \add ≈I've said\add* is right¦321120. You all made¦321126 a solemn agreement¦321127 at my \add ≈temple that carries\add* my name¦321133, that you'd \add ≈monitor each other\add* \add to free your slaves\add*.
\v 16 \add But¦321136\add* then you all turned¦321136 and profaned¦321137 my name¦321140 \add ≈by retrieving\add* your male and female slaves which you'd released as free \add >people\add*, and then forced¦321155 them to \add ≈work as slaves again\add*,
\v 17 therefore Yahweh says¦321166 this: You yourselves haven't listened¦321171 to me—you all should have \add ≈declared your fellow Israelis to be free\add*. \add So\add* listen, I'm about¦321180 to proclaim¦321180 ‘freedom’ for you: freedom \add ≈to experience war\add*, \add ≈deadly diseases\add*, and famine¦321194, \add ≈because\add* I'm going to make¦321195 you a horrible thing in the sight of every kingdom¦321200 \add ≈in the world\add*. That is Yahweh's¦321167 declaration.
\v 18 Then¦321203 I'll¦321203 \add ≈deal with\add* the people¦321206 who've broken my agreement, who didn't¦321212 \add ≈respect the intent\add* of the agreement that¦321219 they established \add ≈in front of\add* me when they cut¦321224 a bull in two and¦321203 walked between¦321227 the \add ≈two halves\add*,
\v 19 \add ≈when\add* the leaders of Yehudah¦321231 and Yerushalem¦321233, the \add ≈officials\add* and the priests¦321235, and all the people¦321237 of the land walked between¦321240 the \add two\add* sections of the bull.
\v 20 I'll¦321244 \add ≈hand them over to\add* their enemies¦321247 and to those¦321249 who \add ≈want to see them dead\add*. Their bodies will be food for the birds in the skies¦321255 and the animals¦321256 on the ground.
\v 21 I'll¦321268 \add ≈hand\add* Yehudah's¦321264 King¦321262 Tsidkiyah \add (Zedekiah¦321261)\add* and his leaders \add ≈over\add* to their enemies¦321270 and to those¦321272 who \add ≈want to see them dead\add*, and to the army of the Babylonian king who's \add ≈attacking\add* you.
\v 22 This is Yahweh's¦321285 declaration: Listen, I'm about¦321282 to order them back to battle against this city¦321289, and they'll capture¦321293 it and \add ≈set it on fire¦321295\add*. Then I'll¦321286 make¦321300 Yehudah's¦321299 \add other\add* cities¦321298 into \add ≈deserted\add* wastelands¦321301.
\c 35
\s1 Praising the faithful Rekavites
\rem /s1 The Recabites; The Rechabites Commended; Jeremiah and the Rechabites; The Faithful Recabites
\p
\v 1 \add Several years earlier,\add* when Yehoyakim \add (Jehoiakim)\add* son of Yoshiyah \add (Josiah)\add* was the king¦321320 of Yehudah¦321321 \add (Judah)\add*, Yahweh¦321314 \add ≈had given\add* Yirmeyah \add (Jeremiah)\add* this message¦321306:\x + \xo 35:1: \xt 2Ki 23:36–24:6; 2Ch 36:5-7.\x*
\v 2 Go to the Rekavite clan and talk with them, then bring¦321331 them into one of the rooms¦321337 in my \add ≈temple\add*, and give¦321338 them wine to drink¦321338.
\v 3 \add ≈So¦321342\add* I took¦321342 Yaazanyah¦321345 (son of Yirmeyah, son of Havatsinyah) and his brothers¦321354 and his sons, and all the \add rest of\add* the Rekavite clan,
\v 4 and¦321366 I took them to the rooms of the sons of Hanan¦321374 (son of Igdalyah¦321377, man¦321378 of God) at the \add ≈temple\add*. Those rooms were beside¦321382 the leaders' room, which was above¦321386 the room of Maaseyah¦321388 (Shallum's¦321391 son), the gatekeeper.
\v 5 Then¦321395 I placed bowls¦321402 and cups of wine in front¦321396 of the Rekavites and told them to drink¦321408 some.
\p
\v 6 \add ≈But¦321412\add* they \add ≈responded¦321412\add*, “We don't¦321413 drink wine, because¦321417 our ancestor¦321422, Rekav's son Yonadav, commanded¦321423 \add all of\add* us and¦321412 our descendants not to ever drink any wine.
\v 7 \add ≡He also told us\add* not to build¦321439 any houses¦321436, \add ≈or to plant¦321447 any crops\add* or vineyards¦321444, \add saying\add* that \add %we\add* must¦321449 \add ≈always\add* live¦321458 in tents¦321452, so that \add %we'd\add* \add ≈have long lives in the land that we're staying in\add* \add as foreigners\add*.
\v 8 We've \add ≈obeyed\add* the voice¦321471 of our ancestor¦321476, Rekav's son Yonadav in everything that he commanded¦321479 us \add and\add* we, our wives¦321488, and our children \add ≈have never drunk wine in our lives\add*.
\v 9 We'll never build¦321493 houses¦321494 to live in, or \add ≈own any\add* \add #vineyards, fields¦321497\add*, or seed.
\v 10 We've lived in tents¦321505, and¦321504 we've \add ≈followed everything\add* that our¦321513 ancestor¦321513 Yonadav \add ≈told¦321511\add* us,
\v 11 \add ≈but¦321515\add* when the Babylonian King¦321518 Nebuchadnezzar¦321517 attacked the land, we \add ≈decided that\add* we must \add ≈move\add* to Yerushalem to escape from the \add ≈Babylonian\add* and¦321515 Aramean armies, so now we're \add all\add* living in Yerushalem.
\p
\v 12 Then Yahweh¦321541 \add ≈gave\add* this message¦321539 to Yirmeyah, saying that
\v 13 Yisrael's god¦321552, Commander-in-chief Yahweh says¦321549 to go¦321554 and \add ≈ask\add* the people in Yehudah¦321557, including¦321555 those who live in Yerushalem¦321559: Won't you¦321555 all accept¦321561 correction¦321562 and listen¦321563 to my messages? This is Yahweh's¦321550 declaration:
\v 14 Rekav's son Yonadav \add ≈told¦321581\add* his descendants not to drink¦321586 any wine \add ≈and they've followed that¦321579\add* to this very day¦321593. \add ≈In contrast,\add* I've \add ≈personally and consistently\add* spoken¦321601 to all of you \add ≈but¦321589 you haven't taken any notice of what I've said\add*.
\v 15 I \add ≈persistently\add* sent¦321609 all my servants¦321615, the prophets¦321616, out to you all to tell each person to turn¦321622 from their wicked \add >behaviour\add* and \add ≈start doing good¦321628 instead\add*, and to \add ≈stop following\add* after¦321633 other¦321635 gods¦321634 and serving them. Then¦321609 they'd live on the land that¦321641 I gave¦321643 to your ancestors¦321645 and to all of you, \add ≈however, you all won't¦321630 listen¦321652 to me or pay attention\add* to me.
\v 16 \add ≈Yes,\add* Yonadav's descendants have \add ≈followed the instructions¦321667\add* that¦321666 their ancestor¦321665 gave them, but¦321668 this people¦321668, refuses to \add ≈obey\add* me,
\v 17 \add ≈so\add* Yisrael's god, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦321679, says this: Listen, I'm \add ≈sending\add* all the disasters that¦321698 I pronounced for Yehudah¦321688, \add ≈including¦321689\add* everyone living in Yerushalem¦321693. \add ≡I'm sending them\add* against them because¦321701 I spoke to them, but they wouldn't listen¦321705. I called¦321706 to them, but they wouldn't answer¦321709.
\p
\v 18 Then¦321711 Yirmeyah told¦321740 the Rekavite clan that Yisrael's god¦321720, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦321718 says¦321717 this: You've all listened¦321724 to the commands¦321735 of your ancestor¦321729 Yonadav and¦321711 have kept¦321730 them all. You've obeyed everything that he commanded you all to do,
\v 19 so Yisrael's god¦321749, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦321747 says¦321746 this: There'll always be someone descended from Rekav's son Yonadav to serve me.
\c 36
\s1 Baruk reads out Yahweh's messages at the temple
\rem /s1 Jehoiakim Burns Jeremiah's Scroll; Baruch Reads the Scroll in the Temple; The Scroll Read in the Temple; Baruch Reads the Lord's Messages
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 In the fourth¦321768 year¦321767 \add of the reign\add* Yehudah's¦321774 King¦321773 Yehoyakim (or Jehoiakim, son of Yoshiyah\add /Josiah\add*), Yahweh¦321782 \add ≈gave\add* this message¦321776 to Yirmeyah:\x + \xo 36:1: \xt 2Ki 24:1; 2Ch 36:5-7; Dan 1:1-2.\x*
\v 2 Get a scroll¦321788 for yourself¦321787 and write¦321791 all the messages on it that¦321797 I've¦321799 told you concerning Yisrael¦321803 and Yehudah¦321806, and all the other nations¦321811. Do this for everything I have said, \add back\add* from the \add ≈time\add* of Yoshiyah until \add ≈the present time\add*.
\v 3 Perhaps¦321821 Yehudah's¦321824 \add ≈people\add* will hear¦321822 about all the disasters that¦321829 I intend to bring on them and then turn¦321835 away from \add #their\add* wicked \add #ways\add*, so I can forgive¦321839 them for their wickedness and their disobedience.
\p
\v 4 Then Yirmeyah called¦321844 Neriyah's son Baruk, and Yirmeyah dictated all the messages that¦321861 Yahweh¦321860 had \add ≈given\add* to him, for Baruk to \add ≈record\add* on a scroll¦321867.
\v 5 Then¦321871 Yirmeyah \add ≈instructed¦321871\add* Baruk saying, “I'm restrained \add ≈from entering\add* Yahweh's¦321883 \add ≈residence\add*
\v 6 \add ≈so\add* you must go and¦321885 read from the scroll¦321888 that you wrote¦321891 at my dictation. On the day¦321902 of the fast, you must read Yahweh's¦321897 messages so that all the people in the \add ≈temple will hear them\add* as well as the \add people from\add* the rest of Yehudah's¦321908 cities¦321910. Proclaim these messages to them.
\v 7 Perhaps Yaweh \add ≈will take notice of\add* their \add ≈pleas for mercy\add*. Perhaps everyone¦321919 will turn¦321918 from their wicked \add #ways\add*, since the anger¦321925 and fury that¦321927 Yahweh¦321917 has proclaimed against¦321931 this \add ≈nation\add* is severe.
\v 8 \add ≈So¦321936\add* Neriyah's son Baruk did everything that the prophet¦321946 Yirmeyah had \add ≈told¦321944\add* him to—he read Yahweh's messages aloud at Yahweh's \add ≈temple\add*.
\p
\v 9 In the ninth¦321966 month¦321965 of the \add ≈next\add* year, all the people in Yerushalem¦321974 and the \add ≈visitors to the city from the rest of\add* Yehudah¦321964, announced a fast \add ≈to honour\add* Yahweh¦321970.
\v 10 \add ≈Again\add* Baruk read Yirmeyah's messages aloud at Yahweh's \add ≈temple\add*, from the room¦321992 of Gemaryah¦321993 (son of the scribe¦321997 Shafan¦321996) in the upper¦321999 courtyard¦321998, by the entrance¦322000 gate¦322001 to Yahweh's \add ≈residence\add*. He did this \add ≈so that all the people¦322009 could hear it\add*.
\s1 The messages get read to the officials
\rem /s1 The Scroll Read in the Palace; The Scroll Is Read to the Officials
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 11 \add ≈When¦322011\add* Mikayah¦322012 (son of Gemaryah¦322015 son of Shafan¦322018) heard all Yahweh's¦322024 messages from the scroll¦322026,
\v 12 he went down to to the \add ≈secretary's\add* room in the \add ≈palace\add*, and wow, all the officials were sitting¦322042 there¦322038: Elishama the \add ≈secretary\add*, Shemayah's¦322048 son Delayah¦322045, Akbor's son Elnatan¦322049, Shafan's¦322056 son Gemaryah¦322053, and Hananyah's¦322060 son Tsidkiyah, \add ≈along with\add* all the \add other\add* officials.
\v 13 \add ≈When¦322065\add* Mikayah reported to them all the messages that¦322072 he'd heard¦322073 Baruk read aloud¦322074 \add ≈for the people¦322078 to hear\add*,
\v 14 the officials sent Yehudi (son of Netanyah son of Shelemyah¦322095 son of Kushi) to Baruk. Yehudi \add ≈ordered\add* Baruk, “Take the scroll in your hand, the scroll from which¦322101 you were reading in the hearing of the people¦322105, and come.” \add ≈So¦322080\add* Neriyah's son Baruk took the scroll and went to the officials
\v 15 \add ≈where\add* they told him to sit¦322123 down and¦322121 read it \add ≈to them\add*, \add ≈so\add* Baruk¦322128 \add ≈read out\add* \add the messages\add*.
\v 16 \add ≈When¦322146\add* they heard¦322132 \add ≈it all\add*, they \add ≈were afraid and¦322131 decided together that they needed to report it\add* all to the king¦322149,
\v 17 and¦322156 they¦322159 asked¦322159 Baruk, “How come you¦322166 wrote down all these¦322172 messages from Yirmeyah?”
\p
\v 18 “He dictated them to me,” he replied, “and¦322175 I \add ≈just wrote them down\add* on the scroll¦322190.”
\p
\v 19 Then the officials¦322195 told Baruk, “Go \add and\add* hide¦322200, and Yirmeyah \add as well\add*. Don't¦322204 let anyone¦322203 know¦322206 where¦322207 you¦322201 two are.”
\s1 King Yehoyakim burns the scroll
\rem /s1 The King Burns the Scroll; Jehoiakim Burns the Scroll
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 20 Then¦322210 they left the scroll¦322217 in the secretary Elishama's¦322220 room and went¦322210 out to the king in the courtyard¦322214 and told him everything \add they'd heard\add*.
\rem /s1 King Jehoiakim Burns the Scroll
\v 21 The king sent Yehudi to get the scroll¦322238, and he went and got it from the secretary Elishama's room. Then¦322230 Yehudi read it \add ≈aloud¦322243\add* for the king and all the officials¦322250 who were standing¦322251 beside him \add ≈to hear\add*.
\v 22 \add *That\add* month¦322259, the king¦322255 was in his winter¦322258 house¦322257 and¦322261 a brazier was burning in front of him¦322264.
\v 23 \add ≈Whenever\add* Yehudi¦322270 had read \add ≈a couple\add* of columns, the king would \add ≈slice it off\add* with a knife¦322275 and¦322267 toss it into the fire until¦322285 the entire¦322288 scroll¦322290 was gone,
\v 24 \add ≈but¦322299\add* neither the king¦322306 or any of his servants¦322309 were afraid¦322300 of the messages (and¦322299 they didn't¦322299 tear their¦322305 clothes¦322305 \add to indicate repentance\add*—
\v 25 Elnatan¦322318, Delayah¦322319, and¦322317 Gemaryah¦322320 had urged the king¦322322 not to burn¦322324 the scroll¦322327, but¦322317 he \add ≈hadn't taken any notice of\add* them).
\v 26 Then¦322332 the king ordered¦322332 a \add ≈relative\add* Yerahme'el, Azriel's¦322345 son Serayah¦322342, and Abdeel's¦322351 son Shelemyah¦322348 to arrest the scribe¦322356 Baruk and the prophet¦322359 Yirmeyah, but¦322332 Yahweh¦322361 had hidden them.
\s1 Yirmeyah rewrites the scroll
\rem /s1 Jeremiah Writes Another Scroll; Jeremiah Dictates Another; Jeremiah Rewrites the Scroll
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 27 After the king¦322374 had burnt¦322373 the scroll¦322377 with the messages on it that¦322381 Yirmeyah had dictated to Baruk, Yahweh¦322367 \add ≈gave this\add* message¦322365 to Yirmeyah:
\v 28 Get yourself¦322391 another¦322393 scroll and write¦322394 down all the messages that were on the original scroll that Yehudah's¦322412 King¦322410 Yehoyakim \add (Jehoiakim)\add* burnt¦322408.
\v 29 Then¦322414 you must¦322420 tell \add @the king\add* that Yahweh¦322423 says: You burnt¦322425 that scroll¦322428, asking why it was written that the Babylonian king would come and destroy¦322441 this land and leave it without people or animals¦322449.
\v 30 \add ≈Now\add* Yahweh¦322456 says¦322455 about King¦322460 Yehoyakim: No descendant of his will ever sit on David's¦322471 throne¦322470. As for him, his corpse¦322472 will be thrown¦322474 out into the heat of the day¦322476 and the frost¦322477 at night¦322478.
\v 31 I'll punish him, his descendants, and his servants¦322487 for their¦322490 \add ≈wickedness\add*. The disasters that¦322505 I've¦322507 threatened them with, \add ≈but¦322480 which¦322505\add* they¦322510 \add ^ignored\add*, I'll \add ≈send\add* onto them and all Yerushalem's¦322496 inhabitants¦322495, and onto every¦322499 person in \add the rest of\add* Yehudah¦322500.
\p
\v 32 \add ≈So\add* Yirmeyah got another¦322517 scroll and gave it to Baruk, son of Neriyah the scribe¦322525. Yirmeyah \add again¦322542\add* dictated all the messages that¦322535 had been on the scroll burnt¦322536 by Yehudah's¦322540 King¦322538 Yehoyakim, and Baruk wrote¦322526 them onto the scroll, \add ≈along with several\add* other similar messages.
\c 37
\s1 Yirmeyah's response to Tsidkiyah/Zedekiah
\rem /s1 Zedekiah's Request to Jeremiah; Jeremiah in Prison; Zedekiah Calls for Jeremiah; Zedekiah's Vain Hope
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 \add ≈By now\add* Yoshiyah's son Tsidkiyah \add (Zedekiah¦322553)\add* reigned¦322550 as king instead of Yehoyakim's son Yehoyakin. The Babylonian King¦322552 Nebuchadnezzar¦322564 had made Tsidkiyah king over the Yehudah¦322569 \add ≈region¦322568\add*.\x + \xo 37:1: \xt 2Ki 24:17; 2Ch 36:10.\x*
\v 2 \add ≈However,\add* \add @Tsidkiyah\add*, his servants¦322574, and¦322571 his people¦322575 wouldn't listen¦322572 to Yahweh's¦322580 messages that¦322581 he'd \add ≈given\add* via the prophet¦322585 Yirmeyah.
\p
\v 3 \add ≈Eventually,\add* King¦322588 Tsidkiyah, Shelemyah's¦322595 son Yehukal, and¦322587 Tsefanyah son of Maaseyah¦322601 the priest¦322602, sent¦322587 a message to the prophet¦322606 Yirmeyah \add ≈requesting him\add*, “Pray on our behalf to our god¦322615, Yahweh¦322614.
\v 4 \add ≈At that time,\add* Yirmeyah was \add still\add* coming¦322618 and¦322617 going¦322619 among the people¦322621, because he hadn't yet been put in prison.
\v 5 Far'oh's \add (Pharaoh's¦322631)\add* army had come¦322632 out of Egypt¦322633, and the \add ≈Babylonians\add* who were besieging Yerushalem heard¦322634 the \add ≈news¦322642\add* about them and \add ≈retreated from\add* Yerushalem.
\p
\v 6 Then Yahweh¦322651 \add ≈gave\add* Yirmeyah this message¦322649 to proclaim:
\v 7 Yisrael's god¦322662, Yahweh¦322661 told me that¦322679 you \add >people\add* should say¦322666 this to Yehudah's¦322670 king¦322669 who sent¦322671 you all to consult¦322674 me: Listen Far'oh's army which¦322679 was coming¦322679 out to help¦322681 you all is about¦322682 to return¦322682 back to its¦322683 own \add ≈country\add*, Egypt¦322684.
\v 8 Then¦322686 the \add ≈Babylonians¦322687\add* will return¦322686 and attack this city¦322691, then¦322686 they'll capture¦322693 it and burn¦322694 it \add ≈down\add*.
\v 9 Yahweh¦322701 says¦322700 not to deceive¦322704 yourselves that the Babylonians¦322710 have left, because¦322711 they won't¦322702 leave,
\v 10 because even if you all defeated¦322719 the entire¦322720 Babylonian¦322723 army that's attacking you so that only wounded men¦322728 were left in their tents, they would get up and burn¦322733 \add ≈down\add* this city¦322736.
\s1 Yirmeyah is arrested and imprisoned
\rem /s1 Jeremiah Is Arrested and Imprisoned; Jeremiah Is Imprisoned
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 11 Then¦322740 when the Babylonian army had left Yerushalem¦322745 \add ≈to avoid\add* Far'oh's army,
\v 12 Yirmeyah left \add *the city\add* to go¦322754 to the Benyamin¦322756 \add ≈region¦322755\add* to \add ≈take possession of a section\add* \add of land¦322755\add* there¦322758 among \add &his\add* people¦322760.
\v 13 \add ≈As he went through\add* the Benyamin¦322766 gate¦322765, a chief guard¦322769 named Yiriyah (son of Shelemyah¦322774, son of Hananyah¦322777) was there¦322767. He seized the prophet¦322782 Yirmeyah and¦322762 \add ≈claimed that\add* he was deserting to the \add ≈Babylonians\add*.
\p
\v 14 \add ≈But¦322790\add* Yirmeyah \add ≈disputed\add*, “That's a lie—I'm not deserting to the \add ≈Babylonians\add*.” \add ≈However\add* Yiriyah wouldn't listen¦322799 to him and he \add ≈arrested\add* him and took him to the officials¦322807.
\v 15 The officials¦322810 were angry¦322809 at Yirmeyah and they \add had\add* him beaten and put in prison. (\add The place\add* had been the house of the scribe¦322822 Yonatan, but¦322809 it had been converted into \add ≈a prison\add*.)
\v 16 \add ≈So\add* Yirmeyah was \add ≈kept there¦322842\add* in an \add ≈underground cell\add* for \add ≈several\add* days¦322844.
\p
\v 17 Then King¦322849 Tsidkiyah sent \add >someone\add* to fetch \add @Yirmeyah\add*, and in his house¦322854, the king \add ≈asked¦322852\add* him privately, “Is there any message¦322858 from Yahweh¦322860?”
\p “There is a message,” Jeremiah \add ≈answered\add*. “You'll be \add ≈handed over\add* to the Babylonian king.”
\v 18 Then Yirmeyah asked \add *the king¦322876\add*, “What \add ≈crime have I committed against\add* you or your servants¦322881 or your people¦322882, that you've \add ≈had me put in prison\add*?
\v 19 Where are \add ≈all the other\add* prophets who prophesied¦322898 to you all that the Babylonian king¦322904 wouldn't come¦322903 \add ≈here\add*?
\v 20 \add ≈But¦322912\add* now, my master¦322916 the king¦322917, please listen¦322913 \add ≈to this appeal\add*: Don't¦322923 return me to the scribe¦322928 Yonatan's¦322927 house¦322926, or I'll¦322930 die¦322930 there¦322931.”
\p
\v 21 \add ≈So¦322933\add* King¦322934 Tsidkiyah ordered¦322933 that Yirmeyah \add ≈be held\add* in the guards' courtyard, and¦322933 he was given a loaf of bread every day from the bakers' street¦322948, until¦322950 \add the time\add* when all the bread in the city \add ≈ran out\add*. \add ≈But¦322933\add* Yirmeyah remained \add confined\add* in the guards's courtyard.
\c 38
\s1 Yirmeyah is placed down a shaft
\rem /s1 Jeremiah in a Cistern; Jeremiah Thrown Into a Cistern; Jeremiah in the Cistern; Jeremiah in a Dry Well
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 \add Four officials,\add* Mattan's¦322968 son Shefatyah, Pashhur's¦322972 son Gedalyah¦322969, Shelemyah's¦322976 son Yehukal, and¦322964 Malkiyah's¦322980 son Pashhur heard the messages that¦322984 Yirmeyah was telling all the people¦322991, saying:
\v 2 Yahweh¦322997 says¦322996 this: Anyone¦322998 who stays in this city¦322999 will be killed by \add ≈fighting\add*, famine¦323003, or \add ≈deadly diseases\add*, \add ≈but¦323004\add* anyone¦322998 who goes¦323005 out to the \add ≈Babylonians¦323008\add* will \add ≈survive—they won't be killed\add*.
\v 3 Yahweh¦323021 says¦323020 that this city¦323024 will definitely \add ≈be taken over and captured¦323031\add* by the Babylonian¦323030 king¦323028.
\p
\v 4 \add ≈So¦323033\add* \add &those\add* officials¦323034 went to \add @King Tsidkiyah\add* \add ≈and requested that Yirmeyah be executed\add* because¦323044 \add (they claimed)\add* his messages were \add ≈discouraging\add* their warriors¦323055 \add ≈defending\add* the city¦323059 and \add ≡discouraging\add* all the people. \add ≡They claimed\add* that he wasn't \add ≈advancing\add* the people's safety, but¦323033 \add causing\add* harm.
\p
\v 5 “\add ≈All right\add*,” King¦323085 Tsidkiyah \add ≈replied\add*. “\add ≈Do whatever you want with him\add*, because¦323091 no king \add ≈can argue against all of\add* you.”
\v 6 \add ≈So¦323099\add* they took Yirmeyah and \add ≈put\add* him into the \add water storage\add* cistern \add carved out by\add* the king's son Malkiyah¦323109. It was \add right there¦323122\add* in the guards' courtyard¦323114, and they lowered Yirmeyah down with ropes¦323120. There wasn't any water \add left\add* in the cistern, but¦323099 it was \add still\add* muddy \add at the bottom\add* and he sank down into the mud.
\rem /s1 Jeremiah Is Rescued by Ebed-melech
\p
\v 7 \add ≈Now\add* the Kushite Eved-Melek¦323137 was one of the \add ≈trusted servants\add* in the king's house¦323142 and he heard that they had put Yirmeyah down into the cistern¦323152. \add ≈Meanwhile,\add* the king was sitting¦323154 at the Benyamin¦323156 Gate.
\v 8 \add ≈So¦323158\add* Eved¦323159-Melek¦323161 left the \add ≈palace\add* and \add ≈went and spoke¦323164 with\add* the king,
\v 9 “My master¦323170 the king¦323171, those men¦323173 have been evil¦323172 in the way they've mistreated the prophet¦323181 Yirmeyah. They threw him into a cistern¦323188 so he'd die in it from hunger, since there's no food left in the city¦323197.”
\v 10 Then¦323199 the king ordered¦323199 Eved-Melek¦323204 to take¦323207 command¦323199 of thirty¦323210 of \add the king's men¦323211\add* to go and¦323199 get the prophet¦323216 Yirmeyah out of the cistern¦323219 \add ≈so he wouldn't die¦323221\add* \add down there\add*.
\v 11 \add ≈So¦323223\add* Eved-Melek¦323227 \add ≈led\add* the men¦323230 to a storeroom¦323239 for clothing under¦323238 the king's house¦323233 where they got some rags and¦323223 worn-out clothes. Then¦323223 they let them down by ropes¦323254 to Yirmeyah in the cistern¦323253
\v 12 and \add ≈told him to use the rags and old clothes¦323267 under his armpits to protect him from being hurt by\add* the ropes¦323273. Yirmeyah did that,
\v 13 then¦323278 they pulled him up with the ropes¦323282—\add ≈that's how they got him up out\add* from the \add mud in\add* the cistern¦323287. Then¦323278 he stayed in the guards' courtyard¦323290.
\s1 King Tsidkiyah's advice to Yirmeyah
\rem /s1 Zedekiah Consults Jeremiah Again; Zedekiah Asks Jeremiah's Advice; Zedekiah Questions Jeremiah Again; Zedekiah Questions Jeremiah
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 14 \add ≈One day\add* King¦323295 Tsidkiyah \add (Zedekiah¦323296)\add* \add ≈summoned\add* the prophet¦323301 Yirmeyah \add ≈to meet him\add* at the third¦323306 entrance¦323305 to \add ≈the temple\add* and told him, “I want to ask¦323315 you¦323317 something. Don't¦323319 \add ≈refuse to answer honestly and truthfully\add*.”
\p
\v 15 “\add Ha,\add* if I tell you the truth, you'll order me to be executed,” Yirmeyah \add ≈replied\add*. “And if I give you good advice, you won't¦323333 \add ≈take any notice of\add* what I say.”
\p
\v 16 \add ≈But¦323342\add* King¦323343 Tsidkiyah privately promised Yirmeyah, “As \add ≈our creator¦323361\add* Yahweh¦323352 lives, I won't execute you or \add ≈hand¦323369 you over to\add* those men¦323370 who \add ≈want to see you dead\add*.”
\p
\v 17 “\add Okay,\add*” Yirmeyah \add ≈answered\add* \add *the king\add*, “Yisrael's god, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦323387 says this: If you indeed¦323394 go out to the Babylonian king's officials, then you'll live, and this city¦323404 won't¦323406 be burnt¦323407 \add down\add*. You and your family would live.
\v 18 But¦323413 if you don't¦323414 go¦323416 out to \add *his\add* officials, then¦323413 this city¦323423 will be \add ≈handed over to the Babylonians\add*. They'll burn¦323427 it \add down\add*, and¦323413 you wouldn't \add be able to\add* escape¦323432 from their¦323433 \add ≈power\add*.”
\p
\v 19 “\add But¦323436\add* I'm afraid of the \add ≈Judaneans\add* who've \add already\add* deserted to the Babylonians,” \add *the king¦323437\add* \add ≈confided to\add* Yirmeyah. “\add ≈You see,\add* I might be \add ≈handed over to them\add* and they \add ≈might treat me cruelly\add*.”
\p
\v 20 “\add @The Babylonians\add* won't¦323464 \add ≈hand\add* you over to \add @those Jews\add*,” Yirmeyah \add ≈responded¦323462\add*. “Obey Yahweh's¦323471 message from Yahweh that I'm \add ≈passing on to\add* you, so that things will go¦323476 well for you, and so that you'll live¦323478 \add through this\add*.
\v 21 \add ≈However,\add* if you¦323484 refuse¦323483 to \add ≈surrender\add*, then¦323481 this is what Yahweh¦323490 has shown¦323489 me:
\v 22 Listen king of Yehudah¦323501, all the women who are left in your \add ≈palace\add* will be taken out to the Babylonian king's commanders¦323505. Those women will tell you,
\q1 ‘You were deceived by your friends—they've ruined you.
\q1 Now your feet¦323517 are \add ≈stuck\add* in the mud, and¦323492 your friends have turned¦323518 away.’
\p
\v 23 \add ≈Yes,\add* all your wives¦323525 and children¦323528 will be taken out to the \add ≈Babylonians\add* and you yourself won't¦323534 escape¦323536 from \add ≈them\add* \add either\add*. You'll be taken captive by the Babylonian king¦323540, and this city¦323546 will be burnt \add down\add*.”
\p
\v 24 Then Tsidkiyah told Yirmeyah, “Don't¦323558 \add ≈tell anyone¦323557 else what we spoke about or you¦323565 might\add* die¦323565.
\v 25 If the officials¦323570 hear that I've¦323573 have talked with you, and if they come and \add ≈demand\add*, ‘Tell us what you said to the king—don't¦323589 hide¦323591 it from us or we'll kill you,’
\v 26 then¦323601 you must¦323601 tell them, ‘I \add ≈was just pleading\add* to the king not to return me to \add the dungeon in\add* Yonatan's house¦323611 \add ≈or I'd\add* die there¦323614.’
\v 27 Then \add sure enough\add* the officials¦323620 came¦323617 to Yirmeyah and questioned him and he \add ≈answered\add* them as the king¦323634 had \add ≈instructed¦323633\add* him. They couldn't say anything else because¦323637 they hadn't heard¦323640 the \add ≈conversation\add*,
\v 28 \add ≈so\add* Yirmeyah remained in the guards' courtyard¦323646 until¦323648 the day¦323650 that Yerushalem¦323654 was captured.\x + \xo 38:28: \xt Eze 33:21.\x*
\c 39
\s1 The fall of Yerushalem
\rem /s1 The Fall of Jerusalem
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 In the tenth¦323669 month¦323668 of the ninth¦323663 year¦323662 \add of the reign\add* of Yehudah's¦323667 King Tsidkiyah \add (Zedekiah¦323664)\add*, the Babylonian King Nebuchadnezzar¦323671 came¦323670 against Yerushalem¦323680 with his \add ≈large\add* army and besieged it¦323682.
\v 2 On the ninth day¦323692 of the fourth¦323691 month of Tsidkiyah's eleventh year¦323688,\f + \fr 39:2 \ft i.e., about eighteen months later (in 586 B.C.).\f* the city¦323695 was broken¦323694 into.
\v 3 Then¦323697 all of the Babylonian king's officials came and sat at the middle¦323705 gate¦323704, \add including¦323703\add* the top official Nevu-Sarsekim, and Samgar¦323710-Nevu and Sarsekim.
\p
\v 4 When¦323733 Yehudah's¦323739 King¦323737 Tsidkiyah and all his warriors¦323742 saw¦323735 \add what was happening\add*, they \add left\add* at nighttime¦323746 through the gate¦323753 between¦323754 the two¦323755 walls¦323755 beside the king's garden¦323751 and fled¦323744 towards the Yarden river plains.
\v 5 \add ≈However\add* the \add ≈Babylonian\add* army chased after¦323764 them and overtook¦323765 the king¦323777 down in the plains¦323769 near Yeriho \add (Jericho)\add*. They took him back up to the Babylonian King¦323777 Nebuchadnezzar¦323776 at Rivlah in the Hamat¦323782 \add ≈region¦323781\add*, and he pronounced \add &his\add* judgement¦323785 on him.
\v 6 The king had Tsidkiyah's sons slaughtered at Rivlah as \add @their father\add* \add was forced to\add* watch, and¦323787 Yehudah's¦323800 officials were also executed.
\v 7 Then¦323805 they \add ≈gouged out\add* out Tsidkiyah's¦323808 eyes¦323807 and¦323810 put him¦323810 in chains to be taken to Babylon¦323814.
\v 8 Then¦323816 the Babylonians¦323825 burnt¦323824 down the \add ≈palace\add* and the \add ≈other\add* houses, and tore down Yerushalem's¦323830 walls¦323829.
\v 9 The rest of the people who'd stayed in the city¦323837, including¦323838 those¦323840 who'd \add ≈previously\add* deserted, were exiled¦323848 to Babylon¦323856 \add under the supervision of\add* the chief¦323853 bodyguard¦323855 Nevuzar-Adan.
\v 10 \add ≈However¦323868,\add* \add *he\add* allowed the poorest people¦323860 who didn't¦323863 own anything¦323866 to remain in Yehudah¦323873—allocating vineyards¦323876 and¦323858 fields¦323877 \add for them to work\add*.
\s1 Yirmeyah is released
\rem /s1 Jeremiah, Set Free, Remembers Ebed-melech; Jeremiah's Release; Jeremiah Remains in Judah
\p
\v 11 \add ≈Now\add* the Babylonian King¦323883 Nebuchadnezzar¦323882 had given an order to his chief¦323891 bodyguard¦323893 Nevuzar-Adan about \add finding\add* Yirmeyah
\v 12 and keeping him safe and unharmed—even to care for him and do anything¦323904 that he requested.
\v 13 \add ≈So¦323916\add* Nevuzar-Adan, the top servant Nevu-Shazban, the high official Nergal-Sharezer, and¦323916 all the Babylonian king's most important officials
\v 14 sent¦323939 out men to fetch Yirmeyah from the guards' courtyard¦323944. They \add ≈handed him over\add* to Gedalyah¦323950 (son of Ahikam¦323953, son of Shafan¦323956) to take¦323957 him home, \add ≈so\add* Yirmeyah stayed \add there\add* among the people¦323963.
\s1 The hope of Ibid-Milik
\rem /s1 Hope for Ebedmelech
\p
\v 15 \add ≈While\add* Yirmeyah had still been \add ≈held\add*in the guards' courtyard¦323975, Yahweh¦323972 had given him this message¦323970:
\v 16 Go and tell Eved-Melek the \add ≈Ethiopian\add* that Yisrael's god¦323992, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦323990 says¦323989 this: Listen, I'm about¦323995 to \add ≈fulfill\add* my messages against¦324000 this city¦324002 for disaster and not for good¦324006, and they'll all come true \add ≈right in front¦324008 of your¦324008 eyes\add* on that day¦324009.
\v 17 \add ≈But¦324012\add* Yahweh¦324018 declares that I'll¦324012 rescue¦324012 you from those people¦324022 that you're¦324025 afraid of
\v 18 because I'll¦324031 definitely save your life. You won't¦324033 \add ≈be killed by the soldiers\add*, but¦324032 Yahweh¦324045 declares that because you put your trust¦324041 in me, your life will be saved.
\c 40
\s1 Yirmeyah returns to Gedalyah
\rem /s1 Jeremiah Freed; Jeremiah Stays with Gedaliah; After the capture of Jerusalem; Jeremiah with Gedaliah the Governor
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 1 The chief¦324062 bodyguard¦324064 Nevuzar-Adan had found Yirmeyah \add ≈chained¦324073 up\add* among all the exiles¦324077 from Yerushalem¦324078 and \add the rest of\add* Yehudah to be taken¦324080 to Babylon¦324081, and had released him at Ramah¦324067.
\p
\v 2 The chief¦324084 bodyguard¦324086 took¦324083 Yirmeyah \add aside\add* and¦324088 told him, “Your god¦324091 Yahweh¦324090 decreed this disaster for this place¦324099,
\v 3 then¦324102 he caused it to happen. Yahweh¦324104 did just as he'd decreed, since you \add >people\add* sinned¦324109 against him and¦324102 didn't¦324111 obey \add ≈him\add*. That's¦324110 why \add all\add* this has happened to you people.
\v 4 \add ≈But¦324121\add* now listen, I've¦324123 released you today from your chains¦324127. If \add ≈you choose\add* to come with me to Babylon¦324138, I'll¦324140 \add ≈look after\add* you, \add ≈but¦324121 if you don't want to\add*, then¦324121 look \add ≈around\add* and¦324121 go \add ≈wherever you think best\add*.
\v 5 \add ?≈Or why don't¦324171 you return\add* to Gedalyah¦324177 (son of Ahikam¦324180, son of Shafan¦324183) who the Babylonian king has put in charge of Yehudah's¦324190 cities¦324189. Stay among the people¦324194 with him, or go wherever \add ≈you think best\add*.” Then¦324170 the the king's chief¦324207 bodyguard¦324209 gave¦324204 him food and a gift, and sent him away.
\v 6 \add ≈So¦324214\add* Yirmeyah went¦324214 to Gedalyah's¦324218 \add place\add* and¦324223 stayed with him among the people¦324226 who were left behind in the land.
\s1 Yehudah's governor Gedalyah
\rem /s1 Gedaliah Assassinated; Gedaliah, Governor of Judah; Gedaliah Governs in Judah
\s4 Southern kingdom
\r (2 Kgs 25:22-24)
\p
\v 7 \add ≈Now some\add* commanders¦324234 of \add Judean\add* \add ≈soldiers\add* who were still in the countryside¦324237, along with their¦324239 men heard that the Babylonian king¦324243 had made Ahikam's¦324251 son Gedalyah¦324248 governor over the land. They also heard that he'd put him in charge of the men, women¦324258, and children who were the poorest people¦324260 in the land—those¦324262 who hadn't been exiled¦324265 to Babylon¦324245.\x + \xo 40:7-9: \xt 2Ki 25:22-24.\x*
\v 8 \add ≈So¦324268\add* they went to Gedalyah¦324271 at Mitspah. Those \add ≈who went\add* were Netanyah's son Yishmael¦324273, Kareah's¦324281 sons Yohanan¦324277 and Yonatan, Tanhumet's¦324285 son Serayah¦324282, the sons of Ofai the Netofatite, and Maakati's son Yezanyah¦324291, and their¦324296 men¦324296.
\v 9 Gedalyah¦324300 (son of Ahikam¦324303, son of Shafan¦324306) \add made a promise\add* to them and their¦324307 men¦324307, saying, “Don't¦324309 be afraid¦324311 to serve the \add ≈Babylonian\add* officials. Live in the land and serve the Babylonian king¦324319, and it will go¦324321 well with you.
\v 10 See, I'm living¦324326 in Mitspah to meet with the \add ≈Babylonians\add* who came to us. \add ≈So¦324324\add* harvest wine, summer¦324337 fruit¦324337, and oil¦324338 and store them in your containers. Live in the cities¦324342 that¦324343 you've \add ≈occupied\add*.”
\v 11 Then¦324347 all the Judeans in Moav, among¦324355 the people of Ammon¦324357, and in Edom¦324358, and in every land heard¦324363 that the Babylonian king¦324367 had allowed a \add ≈small number of people\add* to stay in Yehudah¦324371, and that he'd appointed¦324373 Gedalyah¦324377 (son of Ahikam¦324380, son of Shafan¦324383) over them.
\v 12 \add ≈So¦324385\add* all the Judeans from every place¦324391 that they'd be driven¦324393 into, came¦324396 \add back\add* to Yehudah¦324399 to Gedalyah¦324402 at Mitspah, and they \add ≈harvested a lot\add* of wine and summer¦324406 fruit¦324406.
\s1 The murder of Gedalyah
\rem /s1 Gedaliah Is Murdered; A Plot against Gedaliah
\s4 Southern kingdom
\r (2 Kgs 25:25-26)
\p
\v 13 \add Some time later,\add* Kareah's¦324414 son Yonatan and all the army commanders¦324417 from the countryside¦324420, came¦324421 to Gedalyah¦324424 at Mitspah,
\v 14 and¦324427 \add ≈asked\add* him, “Do you realise that the Ammonite King¦324435 Baalis¦324433 has sent¦324439 Netanyah's son Yishmael¦324442 to \add ≈assassinate\add* you?” \add ≈However\add* Ahikim's son Gedaliah¦324452 didn't¦324448 believe¦324450 them
\v 15 \add ≈so\add* Kareah's¦324460 son Yohanan spoke privately to Gedalyah¦324464 at Mitspah, “Allow me to go¦324468 \add and\add* kill Netanyah's Yishmael¦324473. No one will suspect me. Why should¦324468 he kill you? Why allow all of Yehudah¦324486 that has been gathered¦324487 to you to be scattered¦324483 and the remnant¦324490 destroyed?”
\p
\v 16 \add ≈However\add* Ahikam's¦324497 son Gedalyah¦324494 \add ≈replied\add* to Kareah's¦324503 son Yohanan¦324500, “\add No,\add* don't¦324504 do that, because¦324512 you're¦324515 lying about Yishmael¦324519.”
\c 41
\rem /s1 Insurrection against Gedaliah; The Murder of Gedaliah
\p
\v 1 \add ≈However,\add* in the seventh¦324525 month¦324524, Yishmael¦324527 (son of Netanyah, son of Elishama from the royal¦324535 family) and some officers of the king¦324537 came—he had ten men¦324539 with him. \add ≡They came\add* to Ahikam's¦324546 son Gedalyah¦324543 at Mitspah and \add ≈had a meal\add* together¦324551.\x + \xo 41:1-3: \xt 2Ki 25:25.\x*
\v 2 Then¦324554 Yishmael and the ten¦324559 men¦324560 who were with him, \add ≈stood\add* up and attacked with their swords¦324576. Yishmael killed¦324577 Gedalyah¦324569, who the Babylonian king¦324582 had put in charge of the \add ≈region\add*,
\v 3 and¦324587 they killed all the Judeans who were with Gedalyah¦324597 \add there\add* at Mitspah, as well as the Babylonian soldiers who were there.
\p
\v 4 The \add ≈next\add* day¦324613 \add ≈before anyone¦324619 found out that Gedalyah¦324618 had been murdered\add*,
\v 5 eighty¦324628 men¦324624 from Shekem, Shiloh¦324626, and¦324623 from Shomron¦324627 came¦324623 who had shaved¦324630 off their beards¦324631, torn their clothes¦324633, and cut¦324634 themselves¦324634 \add in mourning\add*. They were carrying grain offerings and incense to \add ≈be offered at\add* Yahweh's¦324640 \add ≈residence\add*.
\v 6 Netanyah's son Yishmael¦324643 went out of Mitspah to meet them, weeping¦324653 as he went. \add ≈When¦324642 he reached\add* them, he told them to come¦324659 and¦324642 see what had happened to Ahikam's¦324665 son Gedalyah¦324662.
\v 7 Then¦324678 as they¦324669 \add ≈reached\add* the middle of the town¦324673, Yishmael¦324675 and his men¦324684 slaughtered¦324674 them \add and threw their bodies\add* into a cistern¦324682.
\p
\v 8 \add ≈However,\add* ten¦324689 of them \add ≈bargained with Yishmael¦324697 about some\add* wheat¦324708, barley¦324709, oil¦324710, and¦324689 honey¦324711 \add ≈that they'd left out\add* in the countryside¦324707, \add ≈so\add* he didn't¦324698 kill¦324700 them along with the others.
\v 9 The \add water storage\add* cistern¦324718 when Yishmael had thrown all the bodies of those¦324750 he'd killed \add ?≈including\add* Gedalyah¦324733, had been dug by King Asa¦324738 \add ≈in defence against\add* Yisrael's King Baasha¦324740. \add ≈Now\add* Netanyah's son Yishmael had filled¦324745 it \add ≈with dead bodies\add*.
\v 10 Next Yishmael captured the remaining¦324772 people in Mitspah, \add ≈including¦324767\add* the king's daughters¦324765 and¦324752 all the others who the chief¦324777 bodyguard¦324779 Nevuzar-Adan had assigned to Ahikam's¦324785 son Gedalyah¦324782. \add ≈So¦324752\add* Netanyah's son Yishmael captured them to hand over to the \add ≈Ammonites\add*.
\p
\v 11 \add ≈Meanwhile\add* Kareah's¦324803 son Yohanan¦324800 and all the army commanders¦324806 with him, heard about all the evil¦324813 \add >things\add* that¦324814 Netanyah's son Yishmael¦324816 had done¦324815,
\v 12 \add ≈so\add* they took¦324821 all their men¦324826 to fight against Yishmael¦324831. They \add ≈came across\add* him at the large¦324840 pool \add ≈near\add* Giv'on \add city\add*
\v 13 \add ≈When¦324844\add* all the people¦324848 who'd \add ≈been captured by\add* Yishmael¦324852 saw¦324845 Yohanan¦324855 and¦324844 all the army commanders¦324862 they¦324866 were \add ≈very relieved\add*.
\v 14 \add ≈So¦324868\add* all \add &those\add* people¦324871 that¦324872 Yishmael¦324875 had captured \add ≈were freed\add* and¦324868 went¦324880 \add ≈back\add* with Kareah's¦324886 son Yohanan¦324883.
\v 15 \add ≈Unfortunately,\add* Netanyah's son Yishmael¦324888 escaped¦324892 from Yohanan¦324896, along with eight¦324893 of his men¦324894, and¦324897 they went¦324897 to the Ammonites.
\rem /s1 Flight to Egypt
\p
\v 16 Then Kareah's¦324908 son Yohanan¦324905 and all the army commanders¦324911 with him, took all the people¦324920 from Mitspah who'd been \add ≈rescued\add* from Netanyah's son Yishmael¦324924 after¦324931 he'd killed Ahikam's¦324938 son Gedalyah¦324935. \add ≡They took\add* \add &those\add* warriors¦324939, and women¦324942 and children and court-officials that¦324921 they'd \add ≈saved at Giv'on\add*,
\v 17 and went¦324949 and stayed at Gerut¦324951-Kimham near Beyt-Lehem, \add ≈getting ready\add* to go to Egypt¦324961
\v 18 because of the \add ≈Babylonians\add*. (They \add ≈worried about their¦324967 response\add* because Netanyah's son Yishmael¦324971 had \add ≈assassinated\add* Ahikam's¦324980 son Gedalyah¦324977 who'd been appointed¦324983 in the \add ≈region\add* by the Babylonian king¦324984.)
\c 42
\s1 The people ask Yirmeyah to pray
\rem /s1 The People Ask Jeremiah to Pray for Them; Warning to Stay in Judah; Jeremiah Advises Survivors Not to Migrate
\p
\v 1 Then all the army commanders¦324993, as well as Kareah's¦324998 son Yohanan¦324995, Hoshayah's¦325002 son Yezanyah¦324999, and all the people¦325005 from the less \add ≈prominent\add* to the \add ≈most important officials\add* approached¦324990 the prophet Yirmeyah
\v 2 and¦325011 \add ≈asked\add* him, “Please \add ≈listen to our request\add*. \add ≡Please\add* ask your god¦325026 Yahweh¦325025 our on behalf of \add ≈all of us who are left here, because¦325032 there's not very many of us left as you can see\add*.
\v 3 Ask your god¦325046 Yahweh¦325045 to tell us what we should do¦325058 and where we should go¦325051.”
\p
\v 4 “\add Sure,\add* I've¦325064 heard¦325064 \add your concerns\add*,” the prophet¦325063 Yirmeyah \add ≈responded¦325060\add*. “Listen, Ill pray to your god¦325070 Yahweh as you've all requested. Whatever Yahweh answers¦325078, I'll tell you. I'll keep nothing back from you all.”
\p
\v 5 ⇔“We \add promise\add* to do everything¦325103 that¦325106 your god¦325109 Yahweh tells us to do,” they told Yirmeyah. “If we don't¦325102, then¦325089 Yahweh can be a true and¦325089 faithful¦325099 witness¦325097 against us.
\v 6 Whether¦325114 it's good or bad, we'll obey the \add ≈instructions from\add* our god Yahweh¦325122 who we're \add ≈asking you to speak\add* to, so that it may be well with us when we obey \add *his\add* \add ≈response\add*.”
\s1 The answer of Master of praying for Yirmeyah
\rem /s1 The Lord's Answer to Jeremiah's Prayer
\p
\v 7 After ten¦325145 days¦325146, Yahweh's¦325150 \add ≈response\add* came to Yirmeyah,
\v 8 \add ≈so\add* \add *he\add* called¦325155 Kareah's¦325161 son Yohanan¦325158 and¦325155 all the army commanders¦325165, as well as all the people¦325171 from the less \add ≈prominent\add* to the \add ≈most important officials\add*,
\v 9 then¦325177 he told them, “You all sent¦325186 me to Yisrael's god¦325183 Yahweh¦325182 \add ≈to pass on your requests\add* \add ≈and¦325177 here's his reply\add*:
\v 10 If you all stay in this \add ≈region\add*, then I'll build¦325199 you up and not tear you down. I'll plant¦325203 you and not pull you all out, because¦325207 I'm upset about the harm that¦325212 I've¦325213 done¦325213 to you all.
\v 11 Don't be afraid of the Babylonian king¦325220 \add ≈any more\add*. This is Yahweh's¦325233 declaration: Don't be afraid of him¦325226 because¦325234 I'm with you all to save¦325238 you and to rescue¦325240 you from his¦325226 \add ≈clutches\add*,
\v 12 because I'll give¦325244 you all mercy. I'll have compassion¦325247 on you, and¦325244 I'll restore¦325249 you all back to your \add ≈country\add*.
\p
\v 13 \add ≈However,\add* suppose that you all decide not to listen¦325264 to the \add ≈words\add* of your god¦325267 Yahweh¦325266, and¦325255 \add ≈decide\add* not to stay in this \add ≈region\add*,
\v 14 \add and\add* if you all say¦325269 that you'll go¦325274 to Egypt¦325273 \add (Heb. Mitsrayim)\add* to live there where¦325275 there's no war, and no trumpets¦325281 \add ≈signalling\add*, and no \add ≈shortage of\add* food¦325284,
\v 15 Now \add you\add* \add ≈remaining people\add* listen¦325293 to Yahweh's¦325296 message¦325294: Yisrael's god¦325304, Commander-in-chief Yahweh says that if you all \add ≈do decide\add* to go \add ≈and¦325291 stay\add* \add down\add* in Egypt¦325313,
\v 16 then the \add ≈war\add* that you all fear will overtake¦325325 you in Egypt. The famine¦325329 that you're anxious¦325334 about will follow you all to Egypt, and¦325318 then you'll die¦325341 there,
\v 17 \add ≈i.e.,\add* \add ≈anyone who decides\add* to go¦325353 to \add ≈live as foreigners\add* in Egypt¦325354, will die¦325357 from \add ≈war\add*, famine¦325359, or \add ≈deadly diseases\add*. There won't¦325361 be any survivors¦325365 from the \add #calamities\add* that¦325369 I'd \add ≈send\add* onto them.
\p
\v 18 \add ≈Yes,\add* Yisrael's god, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦325378 says this: Just as my anger and rage was poured out on Yerushalem's¦325389 inhabitants¦325388, in the same way my anger would be poured out on all of you if you go to Egypt¦325395. You'd become an object of cursing and a horror¦325398, \add ≈something to be used as a curse word\add*, and something dishonourable, and you'd never see this place¦325407 again¦325404.
\p
\v 19 \add Then Yirmeyah continued:\add* Yahweh¦325411 has spoken¦325410 to you all, the \add ≈remaining people\add* of Yehudah¦325414. Don't¦325415 go¦325417 \add down\add* to Egypt¦325418 as you know that I've¦325423 definitely warned¦325423 you all \add against that\add* today.
\v 20 \add ≈Yes,\add* you \add ≈made a life and death mistake\add* when you sent me to your god Yahweh¦325439, and \add ≈asked me to ask him for instructions for you\add* and when you all said that you'd do everything that \add *he\add* says,
\v 21 because I've¦325459 reported \add >all that\add* to you today. \add ≈However,\add* you haven't listened¦325463 to your god¦325466 Yahweh's¦325465 message, or to anything that he sent¦325470 me \add to tell\add* you all about.
\v 22 \add ≈So¦325473\add* now, you should definitely \add ≈be aware\add* that you'll die¦325480 from \add ≈war\add*, famine¦325478, and \add ≈deadly diseases\add* where¦325482 you all wanted to go¦325484 and \add ≈live as foreigners\add*.
\c 43
\s1 Yirmeyah gets taken to Egypt
