\p
\v 1 \add ≈When\add* Yirmeyah had finished¦325490 \add ≈passing on\add* Yahweh's¦325503 messages that¦325505 their god Yahweh had told him to say,
\v 2 Hoshayah's¦325521 son Azaryah¦325518, Kareah's¦325525 son Yohanan¦325522, and all the arrogant¦325529 men told Yirmeyah, “You're \add ≈lying\add* \add to us\add*. Our god¦325540 Yahweh¦325539 didn't¦325537 send you to \add ≈tell us\add* not to go¦325544 \add and\add* live in Egypt¦325545.
\v 3 \add It's\add* because Neriyah's son Baruk is inciting¦325554 you¦325555 against¦325556 us \add so that\add* we'll \add stay here and\add* \add ≈get captured by the Babylonians\add* to be \add either\add* put to death¦325563 or be taken as exiles¦325565 to Babylon¦325567.”
\p
\v 4 \add ≈So¦325569\add* Kareah's¦325575 son Yohanan¦325572, all the army officers, and¦325569 all \add the rest of\add* the people¦325582, refused to \add ≈take notice of Yahweh's¦325584 instructions\add* to \add remain¦325585\add* living in the Yehudah¦325587 \add ≈region¦325586\add*.
\v 5 Then¦325589 Yohanan¦325590 and all the army commanders¦325596 \add ≈gathered all those remaining Judean people together, who'd come¦325605 from all the other countries¦325608 that they'd previously been driven¦325610 away to and\add* returned to live in Yehudah¦325602.\x + \xo 43:5-7: \xt 2Ki 25:26.\x*
\v 6 \add That included\add* men and women¦325622, children, the king's daughters¦325628, and all the people that Nevuzar-Adan, the king's chief¦325637 bodyguard¦325639 Nevuzar-Adan had left with Gedalyah¦325642 (son of Ahikam¦325645, son of Shafan¦325648), and including¦325620 the prophet¦325651 Yirmeyah and Neriyah's son Baruk.
\v 7 Then¦325659 they went¦325659 to Egypt¦325661 because¦325662 they \add ≈took no notice of Yahweh's¦325666 instructions\add* and¦325659 they arrived at Tahpanhes¦325670.
\p
\v 8 In Tahpanhes¦325680, Yahweh¦325676 \add ≈gave\add* Yirmeyah a message¦325674:
\v 9 \add ≈Get\add* some large¦325686 stones¦325685 and \add ≈while the people¦325697 from Yehudah are watching\add*, \add ≈push\add* them into the mortar¦325688 in the pavement at the entrance¦325691 to Far-oh's \add (Pharaoh’s)\add* \add ≈palace\add* at Tahpanhes¦325695.
\v 10 Then¦325700 tell \add @the Judeans\add* that¦325724 Yisrael's god¦325707, Commander-in-chief says¦325704: Listen, I'm about¦325710 to send¦325710 messengers to my servant¦325718 the Babylonian King¦325715 Nebuchadnezzar¦325714, to summon him \add here\add*. I'll¦325711 place his throne¦325720 over the top of those hidden¦325725 stones¦325722, and¦325700 he'll spread¦325726 his \add ≈royal\add* tent¦325729 over them.
\v 11 He'll come here to attack¦325735 Egypt¦325739 \add ≈and he'll kill those that¦325743 I've assigned to die, and similarly for those to be taken captive or run through with a\add* sword.
\v 12 Then¦325750 \add ?≈he'll\add* light a fire¦325751 in the temples of Egypt's¦325754 gods¦325753. Nebuchadnezzar will \add either\add* burn¦325755 them or \add ≈carry them away\add*. He'll clean Egypt out just like shepherds¦325765 pick lice off their clothes, and¦325750 then¦325750 he'll \add ≈quietly\add* leave
\v 13 \add after\add* smashing the stone pillars¦325776 at \add ≈Heliopolis\add* and¦325773 burning¦325789 the temples of Egypt's¦325781 gods¦325785.
\c 44
\s1 Yahweh's message to the Judeans in Egypt
\rem /s1 Denunciation of Persistent Idolatry; The Lord's Message to the Israelites in Egypt; Disaster Because of Idolatry; Judgment for Idolatry
\p
\v 1 Yahweh spoke to Yirmeyah about all the Judeans who lived in Migdol¦325806, Tahpanhes¦325807, and Memphis¦325808 in \add northern/lower\add* Egypt, as well as those in Patros¦325810 \add in southern/upper Egypt\add*:
\v 2 Yisrael's god¦325819, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦325817 says¦325816 that you yourselves have seen¦325822 all the disasters that I \add ≈sent to\add* Yerushalem¦325831 and Yehudah's¦325836 other cities¦325835. See, they're \add just\add* ruins \add ≈today without anyone living in\add* them.
\v 3 \add ≈That's because\add* of the wicked¦325846 things they did¦325848 to provoke¦325849 me to anger¦325849 by going to burn incense and to worship other¦325854 gods¦325853 that¦325847 neither they themselves, nor you, nor your ancestors¦325860 had \add ≈ever heard about before\add*.
\v 4 I repeatedly sent¦325862 all my servants¦325868, the prophets¦325869, to them to tell \add >the people\add* to stop doing those detestable things¦325878 that¦325882 I hate¦325883,
\v 5 \add ≈but¦325885\add* they didn't¦325885 listen¦325886. They \add ≈refused to take any notice of it, or to stop their wicked¦325894 activities like burning incense\add* to other¦325898 gods¦325897.
\v 6 \add ≈So¦325900\add* my anger¦325902 and rage¦325901 was poured¦325900 out and burnt¦325903 in Yehudah's¦325905 cities¦325904 and Yerushalem's¦325907 streets¦325906 \add like a fire\add* and they're \add still\add* desolate¦325910 ruins to this day¦325911.
\p
\v 7 \add ≈So\add* now Yisrael's god, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦325919 \add ≈asks\add* why you all \add insist on\add* \add ≈bringing this terrible\add* harm onto yourselves \add that'll see\add* men and women, children and babies from Yehudah¦325940, eliminated without even leaving a remnant¦325944.
\v 8 You've provoked¦325946 me to anger¦325946 by \add ≈what you've all done\add* with your¦325948 \add own\add* two hands¦325948, by \add ≈burning incense\add* to other¦325951 gods¦325950 in Egypt¦325953 where¦325954 you've all gone to \add ≈live as foreigners\add*. You've cut¦325961 yourselves off so as to become¦325964 a curse¦325965 \add word\add* and a reproach¦325966 among¦325967 all the nations¦325968 in the \add ≈world\add*.
\v 9 Have you all forgotten the wicked \add >things done\add* by your ancestors¦325975 and \add also\add* by Yehudah's¦325981 kings¦325980 and their wives? Have you forgotten the evil committed by yourselves and your wives in Yehudah and on Yerushalem's¦325995 streets¦325994?
\v 10 To this day¦326000, they still \add ≈haven't humbled themselves\add*. They don't respect \add ≈the instructions or regulations that¦326009 I gave\add* them and their ancestors¦326014, \add ≈and so they don't follow them\add*.
\p
\v 11 Therefore Yisrael's god¦326023, Commander-in-chief says¦326020 this: Listen, I'm about¦326026 \add ≈to start working against\add* you all to \add ≈bring disaster\add* and¦326030 \add ≈destroy\add* all Yehudah¦326035.
\v 12 I'll \add ≈eliminate\add* the \add ≈small¦326060 group of Judeans\add* that has \add ≈made up their minds\add* to go to \add ≈live as foreigners\add* in Egypt. I'll do that so that they'll all \add ≈die there¦326051\add* Egypt—from either \add ≈war\add* or famine, \add and\add* from the least to the \add ≈very prominent\add* \add >people\add* they'll die and will become \add ≈a curse word, a horror¦326069 story, and something to ridicule and mock\add*.
\v 13 I will \add ≈punish\add* those¦326075 living in Egypt¦326077 just like I \add ≈punished\add* Yerushalem¦326082 with \add ≈war\add*, famine¦326084, and¦326073 \add ≈deadly diseases\add*
\v 14 \add ≈so that\add* none of the \add ≈remaining people\add* from Yehudah who've gone to live in Egypt¦326098 will escape or survive¦326090 or \add be able to\add* return to Yehudah when they want to return and¦326087 live there. None of them will return except a few who escaped from there.
\p
\v 15 Then all the men who knew that¦326146 their¦326134 wives¦326134 were \add ≈burning incense\add* to other¦326136 gods¦326135, and all the women¦326139 who were in the great¦326142 assembly, and all the people¦326145 who were living¦326146 in Lower and Upper Egypt¦326149, answered¦326123 Yirmeyah:
\v 16 \add Concerning\add* that message¦326153 that you told us in Yahweh's¦326159 name¦326158, we're not listening¦326161 to you
\v 17 because we'll certainly¦326165 do everything¦326169 that¦326173 \add ≈we said we'd do\add*. \add ≡We'll\add* burn incense to the queen¦326178 of the skies¦326179 and pour out drink¦326183 offerings¦326183 to her just as we, our ancestors¦326187, our kings¦326188, and our leaders did in Yehudah's¦326191 cities¦326190 and on Yerushalem's¦326193 streets¦326192. Then we'll \add ≈have plenty of\add* food and will prosper, and won't¦326200 \add ≈experience\add* distress¦326199.
\v 18 Whenever we didn't do those things—not offering incense to the queen¦326208 of the skies¦326209 and not pouring out drink¦326213 offerings¦326213 to her—we were all suffering from poverty and dying from by \add ≈war\add* and famine¦326217.
\p
\v 19 The women said, “When¦326220 we were offering incense to the queen¦326224 of the skies¦326225 and pouring out drink offerings to her, and when we were making¦326223 cakes¦326233 in her image and pouring out drink offerings to her, \add ≈did you think we were doing it behind our husbands' backs\add*?”
\p
\v 20 Then Yirmeyah \add ≈responded¦326240 to\add* all those who'd answered¦326258 him including¦326240 both men and women¦326252. He told them all this message¦326260:
\v 21 Didn't Yahweh¦326281 remember¦326280 the incense¦326266 that¦326267 you all burned in Yehudah's¦326270 cities¦326269 and on Yerushalem's¦326272 streets¦326271—you and your ancestors¦326274, your kings¦326275 and leaders, and the people¦326277 of the land, and didn't¦326263 it¦326282 come¦326282 \add back\add* to his \add ≈mind¦326285 \add*?
\v 22 \add ≈Eventually¦326290,\add* he could no longer bear it because of your wicked¦326294 \add ≈behaviour\add*, \add i.e.,\add* because of the detestable \add <things\add* that¦326298 you all did¦326299. Then¦326287 your land¦326301 became¦326300 a \add ≈deserted wasteland¦326303\add* and¦326287 a curse¦326304, without inhabitants¦326306 as it is today.
\v 23 \add ≈Because¦326319\add* you all \add ≈burnt incense\add* \add to other gods\add* and sinned¦326314 against Yahweh¦326315, and because you wouldn't listen¦326317 to his voice¦326318, his instructions, his regulations, or his \add ≈promises\add*, this disaster has \add ≈come against\add* you as \add you all can see\add* \add ≈today\add*.
\p
\v 24 Then Yirmeyah told all the people¦326342, \add ≈including¦326336\add* all \add &those\add* women¦326346, “Listen to Yahweh's¦326350 message¦326348, all of \add you from\add* Yehudah¦326353 who are \add now here\add* in Egypt¦326356.
\v 25 Yisrael's god¦326365, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦326362 says that both you and your wives¦326369 have said \add ≈out loud\add* and \add ≈confirmed with your actions\add* that you'll all certainly¦326376 carry out your vows to worship the queen¦326384 of the skies¦326385 and to pour out drink¦326388 offerings¦326388 to her. \add ≈So then, go ahead and do those things to fulfill¦326373 your wows\add*.
\v 26 So then all of Yehudah who're staying¦326409 Egypt, listen to Yahweh's¦326405 message¦326403: Yahweh says, listen, I've promised by my \add ≈powerful\add* name that none of the men from Yehudah who're living¦326409 \add here\add* in Egypt will call on my name any more, i.e., you'll all \add ≈no longer\add* say, ‘As \add #our\add* master¦326434 Yahweh lives.’
\v 27 Listen, I'm watching¦326442 over them for disaster and not for good. Every Judean person¦326450 in Egypt¦326455 will \add ≈meet their¦326447 end through war or\add* famine¦326457 until¦326458 they're all eliminated.
\v 28 Then¦326462 \add a few\add* survivors \add from the battles\add* will return¦326464 from Egypt to Yehudah¦326470 \add ≈region¦326467\add*—only a small number¦326472 of them. \add ≈In that way,\add* all the \add ≈remaining Judens\add* who went¦326478 to live in Egypt will know¦326473 whose word will stand—\add ≈mine or theirs\add*.
\v 29 Yahweh¦326497 declares that this will be the sign¦326494 for you all: I'm going to punish you all in this place¦326503 so that you'll know¦326506 that \add ≈what I've said will come to pass, resulting in\add* harm for all of you.
\v 30 Yahweh¦326518 says: Listen, I'm about¦326520 to \add ≈hand\add* the Egyptian king, Far-oh \add (Pharaoh¦326523)\add* Hofra¦326524 over to his enemies¦326529 and to those¦326531 who want to kill him. It'll be the same as when I \add ≈handed\add* Yehudah's¦326540 King Tsidkiyah \add (Zedekiah¦326537)\add* king of Judah over to the Babylonian King Nebuchadnezzar¦326542—his enemy¦326546 who \add ≈wanted him dead\add*.\x + \xo 44:30: \xt 2Ki 25:1-7.\x*
\c 45
\s1 Yahweh's promise to Baruk
