\p
\v 1 This is the message¦326551 that¦326552 the prophet¦326555 Yirmeyah \add (Jeremiah)\add* dictated to Neriyah's son Baruk to have it written on a scroll¦326569 in the fourth¦326573 year¦326572 of \add of the reign\add* of Yehudah's¦326579 King¦326578 Yehoyakim (\add Jehoiakim\add*, son of Yoshiyah\add /Josiah\add*):\x + \xo 45:1: \xt 2Ki 24:1; 2Ch 36:5-7; Dan 1:1-2.\x*
\v 2 Yisrael's god¦326587 Yahweh¦326586 says¦326585 this to you¦326589 Baruk:
\v 3 You've said¦326592, ‘\add ≈I'm not doing well\add* because¦326597 Yahweh¦326600 has \add ≈piled sorrow¦326601 on top of\add* my pain. I'm exhausted from groaning¦326606 and¦326607 I can't¦326608 find \add any\add* \add ≈peace\add*.’
