\q1 they'll be \add ≈handed over\add* to those northern¦327052 people¦327050.
\p
\v 25 Yisrael's god, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦327055 says, “Listen, I'm about¦327060 to punish Amon¦327063 \add the god\add* of Thebes¦327064 \add city\add*, Egypt¦327070 and her \add other\add* gods¦327073, its kings¦327076 the Far-ohs \add (Pharaohs)\add*, and \add all\add* those¦327081 who trust¦327081 in them.
\v 26 I'll¦327084 \add ≈hand them over\add* to \add ≈those¦327086 who want them dead\add*, and \add ≈over\add* to Babylon's¦327092 King¦327090 Nebuchadnezzar¦327089 and his servants¦327095. \add ≈But¦327084\add* after¦327096 that, Egypt will be inhabited as in \add ≈past times\add*. That is Yahweh's¦327105 declaration.
\s1 Yahweh's rescue of Yakov's descendants
\rem /s1 The Lord Will Save His People; God Will Save Israel
\q1
\v 27 But¦327108 you, my servant¦327112 Yakov \add (Jacob, meaning Yisrael)\add*, don't¦327109 \add ≈be afraid\add*.
\q1 Don't¦327109 be dismayed¦327116, Yisrael, because¦327118 listen,
\q1 I'm about¦327120 to \add ≈bring you back\add* from \add ≈far away\add*,
\q1 and your \add ≈descendants\add* from the land of their captivity¦327126.
\q1 Then Yakov will return¦327127, \add ≈find peace, and be secure\add*,
\q1 and there'll¦327131 be no one to terrify¦327132 him.\x + \xo 46:27-28: \xt Jer 30:10-11.\x*
\q1
\v 28 This is Yahweh's¦327143 declaration:
\q1 You, my servant¦327139 Jacob, don't¦327136 \add ≈be afraid\add*,
\q1 because¦327144 I'm with you,
\q1 \add ≈so\add* I'll \add ≈send\add* complete destruction to all the nations¦327152 that I drove you into.
\q1 \add ≈But¦327157\add* I won't completely destroy you,
\q1 although I'll discipline¦327162 you \add ≈fairly\add*,
\q1 and \add ≡I\add* certainly¦327164 won't leave you unpunished.”
\c 47
\s1 The speech of God concerning the ones from-Philistia
\rem /s1 Judgment on the Philistines; A Message About the Philistines; A Message about Philistia; The Lord's Message about Philistia
\p
\v 1 This is Yahweh's¦327173 message¦327171 that¦327169 \add ≈he gave\add* to the prophet¦327177 Yirmeyah \add (Jeremiah)\add* concerning¦327178 the Philistines¦327180 before¦327181 \add @Far-oh\add* \add (Pharaoh¦327183)\add* attacked¦327182 Azzah \add (Gaza¦327186)\add*.\x + \xo 47:1-7: \xt Isa 14:29-31; Eze 25:15-17; Yoel 3:4-8; Amos 1:6-8; Zeph 2:4-7; Zech 9:5-7.\x*
\v 2 Yahweh¦327192 says this:
\q1 Listen, \add armies\add* are rising¦327196 in the north¦327197 \add like\add* floods of water¦327195.
\q1 They'll be like an overflowing river.
\q1 Then they'll overflow the land and everything in it—
\q1 its cities and its \add ≈inhabitants\add*.
\q1 \add ≈So\add* everyone will shout out \add for help\add*,
\q1 and all the land's inhabitants will wail.
\q1
\v 3 At the sound¦327214 of the stamping¦327215 of their powerful horses' hooves¦327216,
\q1 at the clattering of their chariots¦327219 and the noise of their wheels¦327221,
\q1 fathers¦327225 won't¦327222 help their children¦327228 because of their own helplessness.
\q1
\v 4 The day¦327234 is coming that¦327235 will devastate all of the Philistines¦327241—
\q1 to cut¦327242 every¦327245 survivor¦327246 off from Tsor and Tsidon \add (Tyre¦327243 and Sidon¦327244)\add* who wants to help them,
\q1 because¦327248 Yahweh¦327251 is devastating the Philistines—
\q1 the remnant¦327255 who \add originally\add* came from Crete \add (Heb. Kaftor¦327257 Island)\add*.
\q1
\v 5 \add The people of\add* Azzah \add (Gaza¦327263)\add* \add ≈will shave their heads in mourning\add*.
\q1 The remnant¦327266 in Ashkelon's¦327265 valley¦327267 will be \add ≈silenced¦327264\add*.
\q1 How much longer will you¦327271 cut¦327271 yourself¦327271 \add in mourning\add* for?
\q1
\v 6 Oh no, sword¦327275 of Yahweh¦327276, how long will it be until¦327277 you¦327281 stop?
\q1 Get back to your¦327285 scabbard. Stop and¦327287 be silent.
\q1
\v 7 How can it stop when Yahweh¦327291 has commanded¦327292 it,
\q1 when he has ordered¦327292 it to attack Ashkelon¦327297 and the \add other\add* \add ≈cities along the coast¦327300\add*?
\c 48
\s1 Moav's punishment
\rem /s1 The Destruction of Moab; A Message about Moab; Judgment on Moab; A Message About Moab
\p
\v 1 Yisrael's god¦327312, Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦327310 says¦327309 to Moav:
\q1 Nevo \add ≈won't end well\add* because¦327318 it'll be devastated¦327319.
\q1 Kiriatayim has been humiliated and captured¦327321.
\q1 Its fortress has been disgraced and shattered¦327325.\x + \xo 48:1-47: \xt Isa 15:1–16:14; 25:10-12; Eze 25:8-11; Amos 2:1-3; Zeph 2:8-11.\x*
\q1
\v 2 No one will praise¦327329 Moav again.
\q1 \add Their enemies\add* in Heshbon¦327331 plotted disaster against them, \add saying,\add*
\q1 Let's go¦327343 and destroy it as a nation¦327337.
\q1 Madmen¦327340 will be silenced¦327341 \add ≈after¦327342 the sword¦327344 finishes with\add* you.
\q1
\v 3 Listen, a cry¦327347 of distress¦327347 \add is coming\add* from Horonayim,
\q1 where there's ruin and¦327350 terrible destruction¦327350.
\b
\q1
\v 4 Moav has been destroyed.
\q1 Its \add ≈workers\add* have made their cries heard¦327355.
\q1
\v 5 They weeps as they climb Luhit¦327362 hill,
\q1 because on the \add ≈way down to\add* Horonayim,
\q1 shouts of distress¦327372 will heard \add because of the\add* destruction¦327375.
\q1
\v 6 Flee, save¦327379 your lives
\q1 so you'll be like a juniper¦327382 bush in the wilderness¦327383.
\b
\q1
\v 7 Because of your trust¦327387 in your \add ≈practices\add* and your wealth,
\q1 you too will be captured¦327393.
\q1 Then Kemosh will go¦327394 away into captivity, \add ≈along with\add* its priests¦327398 and leaders.
\q1
\v 8 The destroyer¦327404 will come to every¦327407 city—no city will escape¦327412.
\q1 The valley¦327414 will perish and¦327403 the plain¦327416 will be devastated, as Yahweh¦327419 has said.
\q1
\v 9 Give \add ?≈wings\add* to Moav, because¦327425 it¦327427 must¦327427 certainly fly away.
\q1 Its cities¦327428 will become¦327430 a wasteland¦327429 \add ≈without anyone living\add* in them.
\p
\v 10 Anyone who's slack¦327439 doing Yahweh's¦327438 work should be cursed.
\q1 Anyone who's afraid to use his sword¦327442 \add ≈to kill\add* should be cursed.
\s1 Destroyed e the cities of Moab
\rem /s1 The Cities of Moab Are Destroyed
\p
\v 11 Moav has felt secure since¦327447 it was young.
\q1 Its like its wine that's never been poured¦327455 from \add ≈container to container\add*.
\q1 Its never gone into captivity.
\q1 so it \add still\add* \add ≈tastes¦327467 as good as ever\add*—
\q1 its \add nice\add* aroma¦327469 hasn't unchanged.
\p
\v 12 \add ≈But¦327482\add* Yahweh¦327481 declares that \add ≈the time¦327477\add* is coming¦327478
\q1 when I'll¦327482 send¦327482 \add ≈along\add* those¦327485 who'll tip it over
\q1 and empty¦327488 out all its pots and smash¦327490 its jars.
\q1
\v 13 Then¦327492 Moav will be ashamed of \add their god\add* Kemosh
\q1 just as Yisrael's \add ≈people\add* were ashamed of \add the golden calf\add* \add ≈that they¦327497 put their trust in\add* at Beyt-El.
\q1
\v 14 How can you \add Moav soldiers\add* say¦327505, ‘We are warriors¦327506,
\q1 \add ≈powerful fighting\add* men¦327508’?
\q1
\v 15 Moav will be devastated¦327513 and its cities¦327515 \add ≈attacked\add*.
\q1 Its finest young¦327518 men¦327518 have gone down to the place of slaughter¦327520.
\q1 That is the king's declaration—his name¦327526 is Commander-in-chief Yahweh¦327524.
\q1
\v 16 Moav's disaster¦327529 is coming¦327532 soon.
\q1 Calamity is \add ≈rushing towards\add* it¦327534.
\q1
